// raylib bindings, translated from the system raylib headers
// (generated from version 6.0.0; unused declarations cost nothing thanks to lazy checking).
// Covers raylib.h, rlgl.h, and rcamera.h. Link requirements live in
// the build.cx next to this file.
// Omitted on purpose: raymath.h (static inline only, no out-of-line
// symbols), the TraceLogCallback typedef and SetTraceLogCallback (cx
// cannot name a va_list), the GetMouseRay alias (use
// GetScreenToWorldRay), the color macros (RED, BLUE, ... are C
// compound literals, which no cx const holds; write Color(r = ..., ...)
// instead), function-like macros (RL_MALLOC, TRACELOG, ...), string
// macros (pass literals), and the double macros (RL_CULL_DISTANCE_*,
// CAMERA_CULL_DISTANCE_*): float literals infer float32, so no const
// holds them exactly. The rlgl declarations assume desktop OpenGL
// (GRAPHICS_API_OPENGL_11/33): other GL flavors change
// RL_DEFAULT_BATCH_BUFFER_ELEMENTS and rlVertexBuffer.indices.
// C pointers to single items become 'T*?'; pointers to arrays become
// the indexable 'T[*]?' (nullability still matches header imports, so
// header-imported code migrates unchanged).

